# Frontend environment configuration (Vite).
#
# Local development needs NONE of this - `npm run dev` uses the Vite dev
# proxy (see vite.config.js) to reach the backend at http://127.0.0.1:8000
# with zero configuration. This file only matters for a PRODUCTION build
# (`npm run build`) deployed somewhere like Vercel, which has no Vite dev
# server and therefore no proxy.
#
# Vite only reads VITE_-prefixed variables, and only at BUILD time (values
# are inlined into the built JS bundle - there is no way to change this
# after the build without rebuilding). Set this in your hosting provider's
# build-time environment variables (e.g. Vercel project settings), not by
# copying this file to `.env` and expecting it to apply at runtime.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.production   # if building locally for production
#
# Full origin of the deployed FastAPI backend, INCLUDING the /api prefix
# (see app/main.py - every backend route is registered under /api).
# Leaving this unset in a production build is a deliberate, honest failure
# mode (see src/api.js): the app falls back to a relative '/api', which
# 404s obviously against the frontend's own origin rather than silently
# pointing at localhost and only breaking once someone other than the
# deploying engineer visits it.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api
